#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# heaviside_pi

#% text
# `heaviside_pi(x)` gives 1 for |x| < 1/2 and 0 for |x| > 1/2; at |x| = 1/2 it stays unevaluated.

#% text
# `heaviside_pi(x, y, ...)` gives the product.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `heaviside_pi(-1/2)` is written `heaviside_pi(1/2)`. The derivative is `2 dirac_delta(1 + 2x) - 2 dirac_delta(2x - 1)`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
heaviside_pi(1/4)
#% output
#= 1

#% cell
heaviside_pi([-3, -1, 0, 1/3, 1])
#% output
#= [0, 0, 1, 1, 0]

#% cell
heaviside_pi(-1/2)
#% output
#= heaviside_pi(1/2)

#% cell
d(heaviside_pi(x), x)
#% output
#= -2*dirac_delta(-1 + 2*x) + 2*dirac_delta(1 + 2*x)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `heaviside_lambda`, `heaviside_theta`, `unit_box`
